  "body": "Otis Bardwell drives a reconstructed occupied wagon circuit in 1835, and Hans Johnson drives a Brougham circuit in 1904, in Full or Balanced detail. Walk up and use Interact to Stop or Continue; Step back checks visitor clearance. Driver picks and Find use the named person and the vehicle\u2019s current position. Light retires the occupied assembly and restores standing-person ownership.\n\nThe latest pushed increment, `d0671d821ba861a171fbd3394b22e4ed496dceda` (TREE `603f2f88b53ee4a2a2b08d13047383db4ecab221`), improves startup by prioritizing cooperative route continuations and loading eligible assembly code alongside the complete static route proof. Models still wait for route validation. It prepares driver-card code and records without opening UI, and the People pane avoids waiting for the unrelated global building-liberties index while retaining its household, reader, pictures, citations and review flags. Other card tabs retain their original dependency barriers.\n\nWarranted, publication and frame/memory jobs now check out their complete native inputs without unrelated document archives. Full history where required, native commands, decision rules, job limits, quality settings and memory/frame ceilings are preserved. Existing memory repairs preserve scenery; standing Otis/horse refinements and their provenance remain included.\n\nValidation and remaining delivery work:\n\n- The exact pushed TREE passed targeted transport, driven-assembly and Navigator fixtures, native report checks, native publication/validation and five actual-commit QA checks. Normal push and independent Git/PR readback are verified. Full local preflight for this increment remains pending.\n- On actual public HEAD `d0671d8`, the complete frame workflow passed both still-frame jobs, all six ordinary memory jobs and its separate intentional-failure self-test. Desktop memory: 1812 654.39/700, 1835 1258.85/1325, 1904 1230.23/1300 MiB. Phone: 222.64/225, 496.41/550, 398.59/400 MiB. All ordinary memory runs report zero errors. Warranted checkout completed in 5 seconds and chose `bake=1`; content bake is still running.\n- The older `5439723` source passed all four native preflight parts (1,152 distinct checks, 400 self-tests), hosted gate, moving frames and humans. Its published 1835 phone scope C passed driver selection/card/Find/Light restoration. These remain source-specific historical results.\n- The newer 1904 phone scope C still times out at the original visible-card wait. Its post-timeout snapshot contains Hans\u2019s correct card and hydrated census; that is not a passing interaction result. The negative runs are retained. Fresh exact-predicate observation, Stop/Continue scopes and desktop verification remain pending.\n- Current DEV integration is being resolved and checked locally. The PR remains unmerged; the current PR gate has not run while it conflicts. Current-source checks and actual interaction verification remain required before DEV merge.\n\n[Immutable d067 checkpoint and retained failures](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-evidence/blob/0c0db297bc925a10b3fdb1ffe16e55bde3163079/evidence/transport-pr1649-incremental-d067-2026-11-03-2320Z/MANIFEST.json).\n\nThis is incremental driving and interaction work. Broader photographic appearance, anatomy, gait, boarding, riding and natural seated animation remain open. The separate driver look-motion preparation is not included. No broader ticket completion or production deployment is claimed.\n",
